            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Before the new one: say the Tamil for a complication, then the Tamil for to handle."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 1,
          "type": "input",
          "title": "You'll want to know: உத்தி",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "உத்தி — utti — \"a strategy; a technique\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "வெற்றி பெற நமக்கு ஒரு புதிய உத்தி தேவை. veṟṟi peṟa namakku oru putiya utti tēvai. We need a new strategy to win."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Often plural: உத்திகள், techniques."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "உத்தி (utti) is borrowed from Sanskrit yukti, \"union, preparation, application\" (CDIAL 10480); Tamil drops the initial y and makes kt into த்த."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 3,
          "type": "notice",
          "title": "What you've built",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "One more word for saying what happens if."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 4,
          "type": "guided-production",
          "title": "Guided Practice",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "pause",
              "seconds": 1,
